      "parameters": {
        "width": 568,
        "height": 632,
        "content": "## Route incoming feedback to the right team with an AI Text Classifier\n\n### How it works\nFeedback lands in one inbox but belongs to different teams. This template sorts it automatically using n8n's AI Text Classifier node, which sends each submission down a dedicated branch. When someone submits the built-in feedback form, Google Gemini classifies the message as a Bug, a Feature idea, Praise, or Other. Bugs are logged to a Bugs sheet, alerted to the engineering Slack channel, and the reporter gets an empathetic acknowledgement written by a Basic LLM Chain. Feature ideas go to a backlog sheet, praise is shared in a kudos channel to lift the team, and anything else is logged for review. Each category is a real branch, so it is easy to change what each team gets.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Google Sheets, Slack and Gmail.\n2. Point the sheets at your spreadsheet tabs and pick your Slack channels.\n3. Share the form URL.\n\n### Customization tips\nAdd categories like Billing or Security, or route bugs straight into Jira or Linear."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
